Personal Finance Advisor Bot (FinBot)
Project Documentation
1. Introduction

The Personal Finance Advisor Bot (FinBot) is a web-based financial management application designed to help users record, organize, and analyze their personal finances. It combines financial tracking tools with an AI-powered advisor to provide insights into spending habits, budgets, savings, and financial goals.

The application uses Python and Flask for backend processing, SQLite for data storage, and Google Gemini for AI-generated financial guidance. A rule-based local fallback allows the advisor to provide recommendations when the Gemini API is unavailable.

2. Objectives
Provide secure user registration and authentication.
Track income and expenses in an organized manner.
Help users create and monitor monthly budgets.
Track savings deposits and financial goals.
Generate financial summaries, reports, and charts.
Provide personalized financial insights through an AI advisor.
Maintain separation between individual users' financial records.
3. Main Features

3.1 User Authentication

Users can register, log in, and log out. Passwords are hashed using Werkzeug, and authenticated sessions are managed with Flask-Login.

3.2 Financial Dashboard

The dashboard displays key financial indicators, including total income, total expenses, savings, net balance, recent transactions, and goal progress. Charts provide a visual comparison of income and expenses.

3.3 Income Management

Users can add, view, edit, and delete income records. Income sources may include salary, freelance work, investments, or business income.

3.4 Expense Management

Users can manage expenses and assign them to categories such as Food, Transport, Education, Rent, Shopping, Entertainment, Healthcare, Bills, and Other.

3.5 Budget Planning

Users can establish monthly spending limits for expense categories. The application compares recorded spending against the allocated budget and highlights overspending.

3.6 Savings Tracking

Users can record savings deposits, dates, and notes about their intended use, such as an emergency fund or investment.

3.7 Financial Goal Tracking

Users can define financial goals with target amounts and dates, update their saved amounts, and monitor progress toward each target.

3.8 Reports and Analytics

The application generates monthly financial summaries, category-level spending breakdowns, historical trends, budget variance information, and a financial health scorecard.

3.9 AI Financial Advisor

FinBot uses Google Gemini to generate financial guidance based on available user financial data. If the API key is not configured or the service is unavailable, the application can use a local rule-based recommendation engine.

