5. System Architecture

The application follows a layered architecture.

Presentation layer: HTML templates, CSS, JavaScript, and charts provide the user interface.
Routing layer: Flask routes handle authentication, transactions, budgeting, savings, goals, reports, and advisor requests.
Service layer: Financial analytics and AI advisor services perform calculations and recommendation generation.
Data layer: SQLAlchemy models represent users and financial records stored in SQLite.
AI integration layer: The Gemini API provides AI-generated responses, with a rule-based fallback for offline operation.
6. Database Design

The application includes the following principal data models:

User: Account information and authentication data.
Income: Income amount, source, date, and description.
Expense: Expense amount, category, date, and description.
Budget: Monthly budget allocations for expense categories.
Savings: Savings deposits and associated notes.
Goal: Financial targets, target dates, and progress amounts.

Financial records are associated with their respective users to support data isolation. The exact field definitions and database relationships should be confirmed against the model files in the source code.

